XNlcjQ0ODIyODIw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44822820?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke","html_url":"https://github.com/ColinSORourke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-07T18:56:36Z","updated_at":"2026-01-07T18:56:36Z","body":"I tested this a little and dug through the code the other day. My understanding is that `property_can/get_revert` are behaving exactly as intended, they cannot return the correct values for user defined properties unless the user also overrides them in GDScript.\n\nThe Editor Inspector can do reverts even when these functions are not implemented because the Inspector performs an extra step: calling PropertyUtils.cpp property_get_default_value, having to talk to the GDScript Compiler to \"reduce\" the assignment expression to a constant value. \n\nRelevant Code: [Editor_inspector.cpp](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/5d9722e83288f33827bcad70561f0737f8cde456/editor/inspector/editor_inspector.cpp#L790) & [Property_utils.cpp](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/scene/property_utils.cpp#L79)\n\n> If it was intended this way, please add a function for retrieving defaults of regular properties with clear names for distinguishing between them and I would also propose to reconsider that because I think it would be more useful than the current behaviour.\n\nThis could be useful, and there are a variety of ways to go about it - a few of which I'd wager have good reasons they haven't been implemented. However that's the territory of a new feature proposal, not an issue resolution for `property_can/get_revert`","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3720310714/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]